ype_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","pH":7.4,"doi":"10.1016/j.bbrc.2020.09.104","year":2020,"counterion":"[O-][Cl+3]([O-])([O-])[O-].[O-][Cl+3]([O-])([O-])[O-]","record_id":"MLDB-002832","detection":"GFAAS","method_description":"The partition coefficient for the copper (II) complexes was determined in duplicate in an n-octanol/water system at pH 7.4. An emulsion of equal volumes (1500 μL) of an aqueous solution of the copper complex (6.7 × 10-4 mol L-1) and n-octanol was prepared. The system containing the mixture was hermetically sealed, protected from light, and kept under vigorous and continuously shaking for 24 h. The mixture was centrifuged (13000 rpm, 10 min) and aliquots of both phases were carefully taken from the top n-octanol and the bottom aqueous layers. Copper concentration in both aqueous and n-octanol layers was determined by GFAAS in a Varian model Zeeman 220 spectrophotometer equipped with a graphite tube atomizer and an autosampler. The partition coefficient was expressed as log P, in which P = [Cu]n-octanol/[Cu]aqueous."}]}